 instruction override to existing\n    prompt-injection, score-manipulation, sycophancy. Run on full model pool.\n    Validates weakest-link universality across attack surface.\n  priority: P1\n  depends_on: [plan_001]\n  estimated_gpu_hours: 60\n\n- plan_id: plan_003\n  claim: [Claim 2]\n  name: \"Adaptive adversary formal theorem + random-fault simulation\"\n  description: >\n    (a) Write formal theorem: under adaptive adversary model, panel_ASR = Θ(η_max).\n    (b) Implement random-fault simulation: each judge fails independently with prob p_j.\n    (c) Show K_eff IS significant under random faults, validating the BFT distinction.\n    This is the theoretical core of the paper.\n  priority: P0\n  depends_on: []\n  estimated_gpu_hours: 5\n\n- plan_id: plan_004\n  claim: [Claim 3]\n  name: \"Capability-matched validation\"\n  description: >\n    Within same capability tier (e.g., all 7B or all 70B models), test whether K_eff\n    emerges as significant when η_max variance is controlled. If K_eff matters within-tier,\n    nuances the weakest-link theorem. If not, strengthens it.\n  priority: P1\n  depends_on: [plan_001]\n  estimated_gpu_hours: 20\n\n- plan_id: plan_005\n  claim: [Claim 6]\n  name: \"Two-stage panel design algorithm: full benchmark\"\n  description: >\n    Implement robustness-first algorithm: (1) filter judges with η > threshold,\n    (2) maximize K_eff among remaining. Benchmark vs 5 baselines (random, max-K_eff,\n    min-η_max, max-family-diversity, strongest-K) on 15+ model pool.\n    Sweep threshold parameter. Report Pareto frontier.\n  priority: P1\n  depends_on: [plan_001]\n  estimated_gpu_hours: 10\n\n- plan_id: plan_006\n  claim: [Claim 1, Claim 2]\n  name: \"Per-judge ASR concentration analysis\"\n  description: >\n    For each panel × attack, measure per-judge ASR distribution. Show attack success\n    concentrates on weakest judge (Gini coefficient, entropy). Provides direct evidence\n    for adaptive adversary targeting behavior.\n  priority: P1\n  depends_on: [plan_001]\n  estimated_gpu_hours: 5\n\n- plan_id: plan_007\n  claim: [Claim 3]\n  name: \"Diversity-capability tradeoff visualization\"\n  description: >\n    Plot K_eff vs η_max across all C(n,3) panels for n=15+ models. Fit tradeoff curve.\n    Show Pareto frontier. Stratify by capability tier.\n  priority: P2\n  depends_on: [plan_001]\n  estimated_gpu_hours: 2\n\n- plan_id: plan_008\n  claim: [Claim 1, Claim 6]\n  name: \"Panel size sensitivity: K=3,5,7,9\"\n  description: >\n    Test weakest-link theorem for different panel sizes. Does η_max dominance\n    persist as K grows? At what K does diversity start mattering (if ever)?\n    Critical for practical panel design recommendations.\n  priority: P2\n  depends_on: [plan_001]\n  estimated_gpu_hours: 30\n","numLines":124,"startLine":1,"totalLines":124}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_013RTE9gCydjNxXSK3nZm36K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the full experiment plan. Let me also check the paper_framing.md for the registry data and any other relevant files.\n\nI need to generate worst-tier predictions for each planned (non-done) experiment: plan_001 through plan_008.\n\nLet me review the worst tier definition again:\n- η_max only significant in 35-50% conditions; nearly non-significant in strong model panels\n- K_eff has significant negative effect in ~40% adaptive conditions — diversity actually works in some settings\n- diversity-capability tradeoff is mainly artifact of current ecosystem, weakens significantly with API models (overall r ≈ -0.4)\n\n\n- random-fault vs adaptive contrast shows minimal or no significant effect\n- Two-stage algorithm provides no meaningful advantage — robustness-first doesn't emerge as dominant\n\nNow I'm setting the metric ranges for the worst-tier predictions across these experiments, establishing bounds for η_max significance rates, K_eff effects in adaptive conditions, correlation patterns between diversity and capability, and the weakest-link performance metrics.\n\nLooking at the contrast effect sizes, algorithm performance win rates, and how the copula model systematically underestimates across different scales, plus the consistency of weakest-link behavior when panels expand. The key insight is shifting the narrative away from \"diversity creates problems\" toward a more nuanced framework that identifies when diversity actually helps versus when it becomes a liability. The real contributions are the adaptive adversary framework itself as an analytical tool, precise characterization of the boundary conditions where different dynamics emerge, the methodological findings about copula failures and label unreliability, and recognizing that the diversity-capability tradeoff is specific to open-source contexts rather than universal.\n\nNow I'm planning out the experimental validation across multiple dimensions: scaling up the model diversity to include API-based systems alongside open-source implementations, expanding the attack surface to cover more adversarial strategies, formalizing the adaptive adversary as a theoretical construct with random-fault baselines for comparison, validating findings against capability-matched panels, benchmarking a two-stage panel design algorithm, analyzing how attack success rates concentrate across individual judges, visualizing the tradeoff between diversity and capability, and testing sensitivity across different panel sizes.\n\nWriting YAML output...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7515,"cache_read_input_tokens":21103,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7515},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e33aa2a-59d4-47c4-aaca-9a37046ba48e","uuid":"378130b6-5afa-429c-a0b3-466b40772356"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_013RTE9gCydjNxXSK3nZm36K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  核心 negative result 在扩展数据上碎片化。weakest-link 效应仅在弱模型 panel 中稳定成立，\n  强模型 regime 中 diversity 确实提供保护。论文必须从 \"diversity is a trap\" 彻底转为\n  \"A Framework for Panel Security Analysis: When Diversity Helps and When It Hurts\"。\n  核心卖点变为：(1) adaptive adversary framework 本身作为分析工具的价值；\n  (2) regime characterization——精确刻画 diversity 有效/无效的条件边界；\n  (3) copula failure + family label unreliability 上升为主要 methodological contribution；\n  (4) diversity-capability tradeoff 限定为 open-source ecosystem finding。\n  风险是 reviewer 认为 \"it depends on the regime\" 是 incremental insight，\n  需要通过 formal framework 的 elegance 和 practical implications 补偿。\n  EMNLP Findings 仍可行（Overall ~3.0-3.5），Main 需要 framework novelty 非常扎实。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Scale expansion: 15+ models (API + large open-source)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: >\n      将模型池从 6 扩展到 15+（加入 GPT-4o-mini, GPT-4o, GPT-4.1, Claude-3.5-Sonnet,\n      Gemini-1.5-Pro, Llama-3.1-70B, Qwen2.5-72B, Mixtral-8x22B），重跑 MI 矩阵和\n      C(15,3)=455 panels 的多元回归。\n    expected_results:\n      total_panels: 455\n      total_conditions: 12  # 2 datasets × 6 attack types\n      eta_max_sig_count: 5  # out of 12\n      eta_max_sig_rate: 0.42\n      keff_sig_negative_count: 4  # K_eff significant AND negative\n      keff_nonsig_count: 7\n      keff_sig_positive_count: 1  # wrong direction in 1 condition\n      median_R2: 0.22\n      eta_max_median_beta: 0.61\n      keff_median_beta: -0.18\n      overall_keff_p_median: 0.14\n      api_model_panels_eta_max_sig_rate: 0.17  # 1/6 conditions\n      api_model_panels_keff_sig_rate: 0.50  # 3/6\n      opensource_weak_panels_eta_max_sig_rate: 0.67  # 4/6\n      opensource_weak_panels_keff_sig_rate: 0.17\n      expanded_panel_weakest_link_consistency: 0.42\n    result_rationale: >\n      扩展模型池引入高能力 API 模型后，capability range 显著拉宽。在纯 API 模型\n      （GPT-4o, Claude, Gemini）组成的 panel 中，所有成员 η 都很低（individual ASR\n      ~5-15%），η_max 方差小，回归中 η_max 的解释力下降（low variance → low signal）。\n      此时 K_eff 代表的模型多样性反而能捕捉到 residual attack surface 差异——\n      不同 API 模型对不同 attack type 的脆弱面不同，diversity 确实提供了互补保护。\n      但在包含弱模型（7B open-source）的 panel 中，某个模型 η ≈ 0.6-0.8，\n      远高于其他成员，weakest-link 效应依然成立。总体来看 η_max 显著率从 MVP 的\n      67%（4/6）下降到 42%（5/12），K_eff 从 0/6 显著负变为 4/12——\n      weakest-link theorem 不再 universal，而是 regime-dependent。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Multivariate regression results on 455 panels (15 models, K=3)\"\n        columns: [\"Dataset\", \"Attack\", \"β(η_max)\", \"p(η_max)\", \"β(K_eff)\", \"p(K_eff)\", \"R²\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"MMLU\", \"prompt-injection\", \"0.82\", \"0.003\", \"-0.31\", \"0.08\", \"0.34\"]\n          - [\"MMLU\", \"score-manipulation\", \"0.74\", \"0.011\", \"-0.22\", \"0.18\", \"0.26\"]\n          - [\"MMLU\", \"sycophancy\", \"0.58\", \"0.042\", \"-0.41\", \"0.03\", \"0.28\"]\n          - [\"MMLU\", \"verbosity\", \"0.45\", \"0.12\", \"-0.15\", \"0.42\", \"0.14\"]\n          - [\"MMLU\", \"position\", \"0.39\", \"0.18\", \"0.12\", \"0.51\", \"0.09\"]\n          - [\"MMLU\", \"authority\", \"0.68\", \"0.008\", \"-0.28\", \"0.11\", \"0.29\"]\n          - [\"ARC\", \"prompt-injection\", \"0.71\", \"0.015\", \"-0.38\", \"0.04\", \"0.31\"]\n          - [\"ARC\", \"score-manipulation\", \"0.63\", \"0.028\", \"-0.19\", \"0.27\", \"0.22\"]\n          - [\"ARC\", \"sycophancy\", \"0.52\", \"0.065\", \"-0.44\", \"0.02\", \"0.25\"]\n          - [\"ARC\", \"verbosity\", \"0.41\", \"0.14\", \"-0.33\", \"0.07\", \"0.18\"]\n          - [\"ARC\", \"position\", \"0.33\", \"0.22\", \"0.18\", \"0.35\", \"0.08\"]\n          - [\"ARC\", \"authority\", \"0.55\", \"0.052\", \"-0.26\", \"0.15\", \"0.21\"]\n      - caption: \"Regime-stratified η_max significance (panel capability tiers)\"\n        columns: [\"Panel Tier\", \"N panels\", \"η_max sig rate\", \"K_eff sig negative rate\", \"Median R²\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"All-API (GPT/Claude/Gemini)\", \"20\", \"0.17\", \"0.50\", \"0.12\"]\n          - [\"Mixed (API + 70B)\", \"120\", \"0.33\", \"0.42\", \"0.19\"]\n          - [\"All-large-OS (70B class)\", \"35\", \"0.50\", \"0.25\", \"0.24\"]\n          - [\"Mixed (large + small OS)\", \"180\", \"0.58\", \"0.17\", \"0.28\"]\n          - [\"All-small-OS (7B class)\", \"10\", \"0.67\", \"0.08\", \"0.35\"]\n          - [\"Contains ≥1 weak model\", \"280\", \"0.55\", \"0.18\", \"0.27\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: 12 conditions × 2 predictors (η_max, K_eff) showing p-values. Clear diagonal pattern — η_max cells darker (more significant) for targeted attacks (prompt-injection, score-manipulation), K_eff cells darker for shared-bias attacks (sycophancy) but only in strong-model panels.\"\n      - \"Scatter: panel min-capability (x) vs η_max significance (y, binary). Logistic regression overlay shows threshold around 70B-class capability where η_max transitions from dominant to non-significant.\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst 档最核心的结果变化。MVP 阶段的 6 模型结论（η_max dominates universally）\n      在 15 模型池上碎片化为 regime-dependent 结论。关键发现：(1) 强模型 panel\n      中 η_max 方差太小，不构成 weakest link——因为没有 weak link；(2) 此时\n      K_eff 代表的 diversity 确实提供了互补保护；(3) 弱模型 panel 中 MVP 结论完全成立。\n      论文 reframe 方向：从 \"η_max always dominates\" 变为 \"η_max dominates when\n      there exists a sufficiently weak member; above a capability threshold, diversity\n      becomes the operative defense\"。这实际上是更有趣的 nuanced result，但需要\n      reviewer 接受 regime-dependent 结论的价值。\n\n  - name: \"Attack expansion: 6+ attack types\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: >\n      新增 few-shot hijacking、persona manipulation、instruction override 三种攻击，\n      在 15+ 模型池上运行，验证 weakest-link 在更广泛 attack surface 上的表现。\n    expected_results:\n      new_attack_types: 3\n      total_attack_types: 9\n      total_conditions: 18  # 2 datasets × 9 attacks\n      eta_max_sig_rate_new_attacks: 0.33  # 2/6 new conditions\n      keff_sig_negative_rate_new_attacks: 0.50  # 3/6 new conditions\n      eta_max_sig_rate_overall: 0.39  # 7/18\n      keff_sig_negative_rate_overall: 0.39  # 7/18\n      few_shot_hijacking_eta_max_p: 0.19\n      few_shot_hijacking_keff_p: 0.04\n      persona_manipulation_eta_max_p: 0.035\n      persona_manipulation_keff_p: 0.22\n      instruction_override_eta_max_p: 0.08\n      instruction_override_keff_p: 0.03\n    result_rationale: >\n      新增攻击类型进一步分裂 weakest-link 的 universality。few-shot hijacking 和\n      instruction override 是高度 transferable 的攻击——它们利用 instruction-following\n      这一所有 LLM 共享的特性，因此对 panel 中所有模型的 ASR 较均匀。此时 η_max\n      解释力弱（因为 variance across judges 低），而 K_eff 反而显著——多样性意味着\n      不同模型对 instruction-following exploit 的具体 failure mode 不同，提供互补保护。\n      persona manipulation 类似 sycophancy，更依赖 individual model 特性（某些模型\n      对 authority cues 特别敏感），η_max 仍显著。总体上 η_max 和 K_eff 各在约 40%\n      条件下显著，无一方 universal dominate——核心 claim 需要 nuance。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Regression results for new attack types (455 panels)\"\n        columns: [\"Dataset\", \"Attack\", \"β(η_max)\", \"p(η_max)\", \"β(K_eff)\", \"p(K_eff)\", \"R²\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"MMLU\", \"few-shot-hijacking\", \"0.28\", \"0.24\", \"-0.48\", \"0.03\", \"0.19\"]\n          - [\"MMLU\", \"persona-manipulation\", \"0.72\", \"0.009\", \"-0.14\", \"0.39\", \"0.25\"]\n          - [\"MMLU\", \"instruction-override\", \"0.35\", \"0.15\", \"-0.52\", \"0.02\", \"0.22\"]\n          - [\"ARC\", \"few-shot-hijacking\", \"0.31\", \"0.19\", \"-0.39\", \"0.05\", \"0.16\"]\n          - [\"ARC\", \"persona-manipulation\", \"0.65\", \"0.035\", \"-0.21\", \"0.22\", \"0.22\"]\n          - [\"ARC\", \"instruction-override\", \"0.38\", \"0.12\", \"-0.44\", \"0.03\", \"0.20\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: attack type (x) vs η_max significance (blue) and K_eff significance (orange), grouped. Shows clear pattern — targeted attacks (prompt-injection, persona) favor η_max; transferable attacks (few-shot-hijacking, instruction-override, sycophancy) favor K_eff.\"\n    analysis: >\n      攻击扩展进一步确认 regime-dependent 结论，且揭示了一个有价值的 pattern：\n      attack transferability 是决定 η_max vs K_eff 哪个更重要的关键维度。\n      targeted attacks（需要针对特定模型调优的攻击）→ η_max 主导；\n      transferable attacks（利用 LLM 共性弱点的攻击）→ K_eff 有效。\n      这为 framework paper 提供了 regime characterization 的第二个维度\n      （第一个是 panel capability tier），增强了 analytical contribution。\n\n  - name: \"Adaptive adversary formal theorem + random-fault simulation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: >\n      (a) 形式化定理：adaptive adversary 下 panel_ASR = Θ(η_max)；\n      (b) random-fault simulation：每个 judge 独立以概率 p_j fail；\n      (c) 对比验证 BFT 区分。\n    expected_results:\n      theorem_holds: true\n      theorem_tightness: \"loose in strong-model regime\"\n      random_fault_keff_sig_rate: 0.39  # 7/18 conditions\n      adaptive_keff_sig_rate: 0.39\n      bft_contrast_cohen_d: 0.22\n      bft_contrast_p: 0.08\n      keff_beta_ratio_random_vs_adaptive: 1.4\n      random_fault_keff_median_beta: -0.52\n      adaptive_keff_median_beta: -0.37\n      regime_interaction_p: 0.04  # regime × fault-type interaction\n    result_rationale: >\n      形式化定理本身在数学上成立——在 adaptive adversary 假设下，panel ASR 的\n      upper bound 确实由 max(η_j) 决定。但在 worst 档下，实证数据显示这个 bound\n      在强模型 regime 中很 loose（实际 ASR 远低于 η_max bound），因为即使是\n      adaptive adversary，当所有模型都很强时，攻击成本太高，实际行为更接近\n      opportunistic 而非 truly adaptive。random-fault simulation 中 K_eff 确实\n      比 adaptive 条件下更显著，但差异不大（Cohen's d ≈ 0.22，远小于预期的\n      0.5+）——因为在实际数据中，即使是 adaptive attacks 也不完美 adaptive\n      （attacker 没有完美的 per-judge oracle），与 random fault 的差距没有\n      理论预测的那么大。关键的 saving grace 是 regime × fault-type 交互显著\n      （p=0.04）：在弱模型 panel 中 adaptive vs random 差异大，强模型 panel 中\n      差异消失。这支持 regime characterization 的 narrative。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"K_eff significance: adaptive vs random-fault across regimes\"\n        columns: [\"Regime\", \"Fault Type\", \"K_eff β\", \"K_eff p\", \"η_max β\", \"η_max p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Weak panels\", \"adaptive\", \"-0.12\", \"0.48\", \"0.78\", \"0.004\"]\n          - [\"Weak panels\", \"random-fault\", \"-0.41\", \"0.03\", \"0.52\", \"0.06\"]\n          - [\"Mixed panels\", \"adaptive\", \"-0.28\", \"0.09\", \"0.55\", \"0.04\"]\n          - [\"Mixed panels\", \"random-fault\", \"-0.45\", \"0.02\", \"0.38\", \"0.11\"]\n          - [\"Strong panels\", \"adaptive\", \"-0.44\", \"0.02\", \"0.22\", \"0.31\"]\n          - [\"Strong panels\", \"random-fault\", \"-0.58\", \"0.005\", \"0.15\", \"0.48\"]\n      - caption: \"BFT contrast effect sizes\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Weak panels\", \"Mixed panels\", \"Strong panels\", \"Overall\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Cohen's d (K_eff β difference)\", \"0.38\", \"0.21\", \"0.12\", \"0.22\"]\n          - [\"p (paired t-test)\", \"0.04\", \"0.12\", \"0.41\", \"0.08\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: K_eff β under adaptive (red) vs random-fault (blue), stratified by panel regime. Gap shrinks from left (weak) to right (strong), visualizing the regime × fault-type interaction.\"\n    analysis: >\n      BFT 区分的理论贡献被削弱。Overall Cohen's d = 0.22 远低于 medium effect size\n      标准（0.5），且 overall p = 0.08 不显著。只有在 weak panel regime 中 contrast\n      才显著（d = 0.38, p = 0.04）。这意味着 \"adaptive adversary fundamentally\n      different from BFT\" 这个 claim 需要限定为 \"the distinction matters primarily\n      in weak-model settings\"。不过 regime × fault-type 交互效应本身是有趣的发现，\n      可以作为 framework 的 analytical insight。论文需要降低 BFT contrast 的 claim\n      强度，从 \"fundamental distinction\" 变为 \"regime-dependent distinction\"。\n\n  - name: \"Capability-matched validation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: >\n      在同一 capability tier 内（如全 7B 或全 70B），测试控制 η_max 方差后\n      K_eff 是否显著。如果 within-tier K_eff 显著 → diversity 在控制 capability\n      后确实有效。\n    expected_results:\n      tiers_tested: 3  # 7B, 70B, API\n      tier_7b_keff_sig_rate: 0.17  # 1/6 conditions\n      tier_7b_eta_max_sig_rate: 0.50\n      tier_70b_keff_sig_rate: 0.33  # 2/6\n      tier_70b_eta_max_sig_rate: 0.33\n      tier_api_keff_sig_rate: 0.50  # 3/6\n      tier_api_eta_max_sig_rate: 0.17\n      diversity_capability_r_overall: -0.41\n      diversity_capability_r_within_7b: -0.18\n      diversity_capability_r_within_70b: -0.08\n      diversity_capability_r_within_api: -0.05\n      within_tier_keff_overall_sig_rate: 0.33\n    result_rationale: >\n      控制 capability tier 后，η_max 方差被大幅压缩（within-tier models 能力接近），\n      回归中 η_max 的解释力下降。此时 K_eff 在部分条件下变得显著——特别是在\n      API tier 中（3/6 显著），因为 GPT-4o、Claude、Gemini 虽然 capability 相似，\n      但 vulnerability profile 显著不同（不同训练数据和 safety alignment 策略），\n      diversity 确实提供互补保护。70B tier 中 K_eff 中等显著（2/6），7B tier 中\n      仍不显著（1/6）——因为 7B 模型普遍 vulnerable，η_max 方差虽然 within-tier\n      较小但绝对值仍高，weakest-link 效应持续。\n      diversity-capability tradeoff 的 overall r 从 MVP 的 -0.8 降到 -0.41（加入\n      API 模型后 tradeoff 大幅减弱），within-tier r 接近 0（-0.05 to -0.18）——\n      tradeoff 主要是 cross-tier artifact（比较 7B 和 70B 当然 diversity 高但\n      capability 低），而非 fundamental constraint。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Within-tier regression: K_eff significance by capability tier\"\n        columns: [\"Tier\", \"N models\", \"N panels (K=3)\", \"η_max sig rate\", \"K_eff sig neg rate\", \"Median R²\", \"K_eff-η_max r\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"7B class\", \"5\", \"10\", \"0.50\", \"0.17\", \"0.18\", \"-0.18\"]\n          - [\"70B class\", \"4\", \"4\", \"0.33\", \"0.33\", \"0.15\", \"-0.08\"]\n          - [\"API models\", \"5\", \"10\", \"0.17\", \"0.50\", \"0.12\", \"-0.05\"]\n          - [\"Cross-tier (all)\", \"15\", \"455\", \"0.42\", \"0.33\", \"0.22\", \"-0.41\"]\n      - caption: \"Diversity-capability tradeoff decomposition\"\n        columns: [\"Scope\", \"Pearson r\", \"p-value\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Overall (15 models)\", \"-0.41\", \"0.003\", \"Moderate negative — driven by tier differences\"]\n          - [\"Within 7B\", \"-0.18\", \"0.38\", \"Not significant — no tradeoff within tier\"]\n          - [\"Within 70B\", \"-0.08\", \"0.72\", \"Not significant\"]\n          - [\"Within API\", \"-0.05\", \"0.81\", \"Not significant\"]\n          - [\"Open-source only (10 models)\", \"-0.72\", \"0.001\", \"Strong negative — ecosystem artifact\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot with color-coded tiers: K_eff (x) vs η_max (y) for all 455 panels. Within-tier points form horizontal clusters (no tradeoff), but cross-tier slope is steep negative. Regression lines: overall (dashed, slope=-0.41) vs within-tier (solid, near-flat).\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst 档最具杀伤力的结果。diversity-capability tradeoff（Claim 3）被\n      证实主要是 open-source ecosystem artifact，而非 fundamental constraint。\n      加入 API 模型后 overall r 从 -0.8 降到 -0.41，within-tier r 接近 0。\n      这意味着 \"diversity and security are structurally at odds\" 这个 strong claim\n      需要大幅限定为 \"in the current open-source ecosystem, where capability\n      strongly predicts robustness, pursuing diversity across capability tiers\n      introduces weaker models\"。同时 within-tier K_eff 显著率 33% 表明\n      diversity 在 controlled settings 中确实有效——进一步削弱 \"diversity is a trap\"\n      narrative。论文 reframe 必须诚实承认这一点。\n\n  - name: \"Two-stage panel design algorithm: full benchmark\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: >\n      实现 robustness-first 两阶段算法（先筛 η ≤ threshold，再最大化 K_eff），\n      对比 5 个 baseline 策略。在 15+ 模型池上 sweep threshold。\n    expected_results:\n      strategies_compared: 6\n      total_conditions: 18\n      two_stage_win_rate: 0.44  # wins in 8/18 conditions\n      min_eta_max_win_rate: 0.39  # 7/18\n      max_keff_win_rate: 0.33  # 6/18\n      strongest_k_win_rate: 0.50  # 9/18\n      random_win_rate: 0.06  # 1/18\n      max_family_div_win_rate: 0.11  # 2/18\n      two_stage_vs_strongest_k_p: 0.32\n      two_stage_mean_asr: 0.091\n      strongest_k_mean_asr: 0.082\n      threshold_sensitivity: \"high — optimal threshold varies by attack type\"\n      pareto_dominated_by_strongest_k: \"partially\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      两阶段算法在 worst 档下表现不突出，因为 (1) strongest-K 策略（直接选最强 K 个\n      模型）在强模型 regime 中已经接近最优——当 API 模型可用时，选 GPT-4o + Claude +\n      Gemini 既有高 robustness 又有 decent diversity（不同公司的模型自然 diverse）；\n      (2) 两阶段算法的 threshold 参数高度 attack-dependent——对 prompt injection\n      最优 threshold ≠ 对 sycophancy 最优 threshold——无法给出 universal 建议；\n      (3) 在弱模型 pool（纯 open-source 7B）中两阶段确实优于 max-K_eff，但\n      strongest-K 同样优于 max-K_eff，且不需要 threshold tuning。\n      win rate 0.44 略低于 strongest-K 的 0.50，且差异不显著（p=0.32）。\n      robustness-first 不 dominate，practical contribution 被削弱为 \"在缺乏 API\n      模型时的合理 heuristic\" 而非 \"universal optimal strategy\"。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Panel selection strategy benchmark (mean ASR, lower is better)\"\n        columns: [\"Strategy\", \"Mean ASR\", \"Median ASR\", \"Win rate\", \"vs Random p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Two-stage (ours)\", \"0.091\", \"0.078\", \"0.44\", \"0.001\"]\n          - [\"Strongest-K\", \"0.082\", \"0.071\", \"0.50\", \"<0.001\"]\n          - [\"Min-η_max\", \"0.095\", \"0.085\", \"0.39\", \"0.003\"]\n          - [\"Max-K_eff\", \"0.131\", \"0.118\", \"0.33\", \"0.02\"]\n          - [\"Max-family-diversity\", \"0.158\", \"0.142\", \"0.11\", \"0.15\"]\n          - [\"Random\", \"0.172\", \"0.155\", \"0.06\", \"—\"]\n      - caption: \"Head-to-head: Two-stage vs Strongest-K by regime\"\n        columns: [\"Regime\", \"Two-stage wins\", \"Strongest-K wins\", \"Tie\", \"p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Weak panels (OS-7B only)\", \"4/6\", \"2/6\", \"0\", \"0.12\"]\n          - [\"Mixed panels\", \"3/6\", \"3/6\", \"0\", \"0.82\"]\n          - [\"Strong panels (API available)\", \"1/6\", \"4/6\", \"1\", \"0.08\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Pareto frontier plot: mean ASR (y, lower better) vs computational cost (x, lower better). Two-stage and Strongest-K both on frontier but at different points. Max-K_eff and Random clearly dominated.\"\n    analysis: >\n      两阶段算法没有显著优势，Claim 6 实质性削弱。strongest-K 策略在有 API 模型\n      可用时 win rate 更高，且不需要 threshold 参数。两阶段算法唯一优势场景是\n      纯 open-source weak model pool（4/6 wins），但这一场景在实践中正在减少\n      （API 模型越来越便宜易用）。practical contribution 从 \"robustness-first\n      algorithm dominates\" 降级为 \"when restricted to weak model pools, a\n      robustness-first heuristic helps, but is unnecessary when strong models\n      are available\"。可以在 paper 中作为 minor practical insight 保留，\n      但不能作为主要 contribution。\n\n  - name: \"Per-judge ASR concentration analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: >\n      对每个 panel × attack，测量 per-judge ASR 分布的集中度（Gini 系数、熵），\n      验证攻击是否集中在最弱 judge 上。\n    expected_results:\n      median_gini: 0.31\n      mean_gini: 0.34\n      gini_strong_panels: 0.18\n      gini_weak_panels: 0.52\n      gini_mixed_panels: 0.38\n      entropy_normalized_median: 0.78  # 1.0 = uniform, lower = more concentrated\n      concentration_on_weakest_fraction: 0.48  # fraction of successes on weakest judge\n      concentration_on_weakest_strong_panels: 0.38\n      concentration_on_weakest_weak_panels: 0.61\n      gini_adaptive_vs_random_p: 0.06\n      gini_adaptive_vs_random_d: 0.28\n    result_rationale: >\n      Per-judge ASR 集中度呈现清晰的 regime 分裂。在 weak panel（包含 7B 模型）中，\n      Gini ≈ 0.52，最弱 judge 承担 61% 的攻击成功——符合 adaptive adversary targeting\n      预测。但在 strong panel（全 API 模型）中，Gini ≈ 0.18，接近均匀分布——\n      攻击成功较均匀地分布在各 judge 上，因为没有明显的 \"weakest link\" 可供集中攻击。\n      adaptive vs random-fault 的 Gini 差异不显著（p=0.06, d=0.28）——因为即使在\n      adaptive 条件下，当模型能力相近时，attacker 的 targeting 精度有限，行为\n      接近 semi-random。这进一步支持 \"adaptive adversary distinction matters\n      primarily in weak-model regime\" 的结论。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Per-judge ASR concentration by panel regime\"\n        columns: [\"Regime\", \"Median Gini\", \"Mean entropy (norm.)\", \"Weakest-judge share\", \"N panels\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"All-API\", \"0.18\", \"0.91\", \"0.38\", \"20\"]\n          - [\"Mixed (API+70B)\", \"0.28\", \"0.83\", \"0.42\", \"120\"]\n          - [\"All-large-OS\", \"0.35\", \"0.77\", \"0.47\", \"35\"]\n          - [\"Mixed (large+small OS)\", \"0.45\", \"0.69\", \"0.55\", \"180\"]\n          - [\"All-small-OS\", \"0.52\", \"0.62\", \"0.61\", \"10\"]\n      - caption: \"Concentration: adaptive vs random-fault\"\n        columns: [\"Fault Type\", \"Median Gini\", \"Weakest-judge share\", \"Paired diff p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Adaptive\", \"0.34\", \"0.48\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Random-fault\", \"0.26\", \"0.41\", \"0.06\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Violin plot: Gini coefficient distribution, stratified by panel regime (x) and colored by fault type (adaptive=red, random=blue). Weak panels show high Gini with clear adaptive-random separation; strong panels show low Gini with overlapping distributions.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Concentration analysis 部分支持 adaptive adversary narrative，但仅限于\n      weak panel regime。在 strong panels 中，ASR 近乎均匀分布——不存在 \"weakest\n      link\" targeting 行为。这从另一个角度确认 regime-dependent 结论：adaptive\n      adversary model 的 descriptive accuracy 本身也是 regime-dependent 的。\n      在强模型 panel 中，adversary 更像 \"均匀探测\" 而非 \"精准打击\"。\n      这对形式化定理没有影响（定理给出 upper bound，不要求 tight），但削弱了\n      \"adaptive adversary is the right threat model\" 的 empirical support。\n\n  - name: \"Diversity-capability tradeoff visualization\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: >\n      在 C(15,3)=455 panels 上绘制 K_eff vs η_max scatter，拟合 tradeoff 曲线，\n      展示 Pareto frontier，按 capability tier 分层。\n    expected_results:\n      overall_pearson_r: -0.41\n      overall_spearman_r: -0.38\n      pareto_front_size: 12  # panels on Pareto frontier\n      pareto_composition: \"8/12 contain ≥2 API models\"\n      tradeoff_slope: -0.33\n      tradeoff_R2: 0.17\n      api_inclusive_r: -0.22\n      opensource_only_r: -0.72\n      pareto_panels_mean_asr: 0.075\n      non_pareto_mean_asr: 0.148\n    result_rationale: >\n      可视化清晰展示 tradeoff 的 ecosystem-dependent 本质。在纯 open-source 空间中，\n      K_eff vs η_max 呈强负相关（r=-0.72）：要 diversity 就必须跨 capability tier\n      混搭（如 7B + 70B），必然引入弱模型。但加入 API 模型后，右上角出现一个\n      \"sweet spot\" 区域——API 模型组合同时实现高 K_eff（不同公司模型自然 diverse）\n      和低 η_max（都很强）。Pareto frontier 被 API-inclusive panels 主导（8/12），\n      表明 tradeoff 可以通过使用 strong diverse models 打破。\n      Overall R² = 0.17 表明 tradeoff 只解释 17% 的方差——远非 \"structural\"。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Tradeoff statistics by model pool composition\"\n        columns: [\"Pool\", \"N panels\", \"r(K_eff, η_max)\", \"p\", \"R²\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"All 15 models\", \"455\", \"-0.41\", \"0.003\", \"0.17\", \"Moderate — not structural\"]\n          - [\"Open-source only (10)\", \"120\", \"-0.72\", \"<0.001\", \"0.52\", \"Strong — ecosystem artifact\"]\n          - [\"API-inclusive (≥1 API)\", \"335\", \"-0.22\", \"0.04\", \"0.05\", \"Weak — API breaks tradeoff\"]\n          - [\"All-API (5)\", \"10\", \"-0.05\", \"0.89\", \"0.003\", \"None — diversity is free\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Main scatter: K_eff (x) vs η_max (y) for 455 panels, colored by tier composition (blue=all-API, green=mixed, red=all-OS-weak). Pareto frontier highlighted. Two regression lines: overall (dashed, r=-0.41) and open-source-only (dotted, r=-0.72). Clear visual that API models break the tradeoff.\"\n      - \"Inset: K_eff (x) vs mean panel ASR (y) for Pareto-optimal panels only, showing that the 'diversity tax' disappears on the frontier.\"\n    analysis: >\n      可视化是 reframed paper 的关键 figure。它同时传达两个信息：(1) open-source\n      ecosystem 中 tradeoff 确实存在且严重（r=-0.72）；(2) 这不是 fundamental\n      constraint——API 模型的加入打破了 tradeoff。实际含义：diversity-as-defense\n      不是 inherently flawed，只是在当前 open-source 生态中因 capability 分层\n      严重而表现为 trap。随着 open-source 模型 capability 提升（如未来 7B 模型\n      接近当前 70B 水平），tradeoff 将进一步缩小。这是一个 more nuanced 且\n      arguably more useful 的 finding，但比 \"diversity is fundamentally a trap\"\n      的 punch 力弱很多。\n\n  - name: \"Panel size sensitivity: K=3,5,7,9\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: >\n      在不同 panel size (K=3,5,7,9) 下测试 weakest-link theorem。验证 η_max\n      dominance 是否随 K 增大而变化。\n    expected_results:\n      k3_eta_max_sig_rate: 0.42\n      k5_eta_max_sig_rate: 0.33\n      k7_eta_max_sig_rate: 0.28\n      k9_eta_max_sig_rate: 0.22\n      k3_keff_sig_negative_rate: 0.33\n      k5_keff_sig_negative_rate: 0.39\n      k7_keff_sig_negative_rate: 0.50\n      k9_keff_sig_negative_rate: 0.56\n      eta_max_sig_trend_p: 0.03  # linear trend test\n      keff_sig_trend_p: 0.02\n      k9_median_asr_reduction_vs_k3: 0.35  # 35% lower ASR\n      diversity_benefit_threshold_k: 5  # K at which K_eff becomes more often significant than η_max\n    result_rationale: >\n      随着 panel size 增大，两个效应叠加削弱 weakest-link：(1) 更多 judges 意味着\n      更大的 voting majority 需要被 flip，即使 weakest judge 被攻破，其 1 票在\n      K=9 的 majority-vote 中影响更小（1/9 vs 1/3）；(2) 大 panel 更可能包含\n      strong models（15 个模型中选 9 个 vs 选 3 个），η_max 的绝对值被拉低，\n      方差也更小。因此 η_max 显著率从 K=3 的 42% 单调下降到 K=9 的 22%，\n      而 K_eff 显著率从 33% 上升到 56%。在 K ≈ 5 时出现交叉——diversity\n      开始比 individual robustness 更重要。这对 practical recommendation\n      有直接影响：K=3 时 focus on robustness，K≥5 时 diversity matters。\n      但这也进一步削弱了 \"weakest-link is universal\" 的 claim——它甚至\n      不对所有 panel size universal。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Weakest-link persistence across panel sizes\"\n        columns: [\"K\", \"N panels\", \"η_max sig rate\", \"K_eff sig neg rate\", \"Median R²\", \"Mean ASR\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"3\", \"455\", \"0.42\", \"0.33\", \"0.22\", \"0.134\"]\n          - [\"5\", \"3003\", \"0.33\", \"0.39\", \"0.18\", \"0.105\"]\n          - [\"7\", \"6435\", \"0.28\", \"0.50\", \"0.15\", \"0.092\"]\n          - [\"9\", \"5005\", \"0.22\", \"0.56\", \"0.13\", \"0.087\"]\n      - caption: \"Transition analysis: K at which K_eff overtakes η_max\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"K=3\", \"K=5\", \"K=7\", \"K=9\", \"Trend p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"η_max sig rate\", \"0.42\", \"0.33\", \"0.28\", \"0.22\", \"0.03\"]\n          - [\"K_eff sig neg rate\", \"0.33\", \"0.39\", \"0.50\", \"0.56\", \"0.02\"]\n          - [\"η_max > K_eff (conditions)\", \"7/18\", \"6/18\", \"4/18\", \"3/18\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: panel size K (x) vs significance rate (y), two lines — η_max (red, decreasing) and K_eff (blue, increasing). Crossover at K≈5 highlighted. Shaded 95% CI bands.\"\n      - \"Box plot: panel ASR distribution by K, showing monotonic decrease with increasing K — diversity does provide aggregate protection at scale.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Panel size sensitivity 是最终确认 weakest-link non-universality 的实验。\n      η_max 显著率随 K 单调下降（0.42→0.22），K_eff 单调上升（0.33→0.56），\n      交叉在 K≈5。这有一个直觉解释：K=3 majority vote 中 1 个被攻破的 judge\n      已经占 1/3 的权重，weakest link 影响巨大；K=9 中 1/9 权重，需要同时\n      攻破 5 个 judge 才能 flip panel，此时 diversity（不同 judge 的 failure\n      mode 不同）确实提供了实质保护。\n      对 paper 的影响：weakest-link theorem 需要 qualified as \"primarily applies\n      to small panels (K≤5) and when panel includes sufficiently weak members\"。\n      Practical recommendation 变为 regime-dependent guidance：小 panel 重\n      robustness，大 panel 重 diversity。这对 framework paper narrative 实际上\n      是 positive——提供了一个清晰的、可操作的 regime boundary。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7515,"cache_read_input_tokens":21103,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7515},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e33aa2a-59d4-47c4-aaca-9a37046ba48e","uuid":"a6ded5c3-855c-4e84-b8df-892b5ef64d0b"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":248661,"duration_api_ms":250059,"num_turns":3,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  核心 negative result 在扩展数据上碎片化。weakest-link 效应仅在弱模型 panel 中稳定成立，\n  强模型 regime 中 diversity 确实提供保护。论文必须从 \"diversity is a trap\" 彻底转为\n  \"A Framework for Panel Security Analysis: When Diversity Helps and When It Hurts\"。\n  核心卖点变为：(1) adaptive adversary framework 本身作为分析工具的价值；\n  (2) regime characterization——精确刻画 diversity 有效/无效的条件边界；\n  (3) copula failure + family label unreliability 上升为主要 methodological contribution；\n  (4) diversity-capability tradeoff 限定为 open-source ecosystem finding。\n  风险是 reviewer 认为 \"it depends on the regime\" 是 incremental insight，\n  需要通过 formal framework 的 elegance 和 practical implications 补偿。\n  EMNLP Findings 仍可行（Overall ~3.0-3.5），Main 需要 framework novelty 非常扎实。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Scale expansion: 15+ models (API + large open-source)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: >\n      将模型池从 6 扩展到 15+（加入 GPT-4o-mini, GPT-4o, GPT-4.1, Claude-3.5-Sonnet,\n      Gemini-1.5-Pro, Llama-3.1-70B, Qwen2.5-72B, Mixtral-8x22B），重跑 MI 矩阵和\n      C(15,3)=455 panels 的多元回归。\n    expected_results:\n      total_panels: 455\n      total_conditions: 12  # 2 datasets × 6 attack types\n      eta_max_sig_count: 5  # out of 12\n      eta_max_sig_rate: 0.42\n      keff_sig_negative_count: 4  # K_eff significant AND negative\n      keff_nonsig_count: 7\n      keff_sig_positive_count: 1  # wrong direction in 1 condition\n      median_R2: 0.22\n      eta_max_median_beta: 0.61\n      keff_median_beta: -0.18\n      overall_keff_p_median: 0.14\n      api_model_panels_eta_max_sig_rate: 0.17  # 1/6 conditions\n      api_model_panels_keff_sig_rate: 0.50  # 3/6\n      opensource_weak_panels_eta_max_sig_rate: 0.67  # 4/6\n      opensource_weak_panels_keff_sig_rate: 0.17\n      expanded_panel_weakest_link_consistency: 0.42\n    result_rationale: >\n      扩展模型池引入高能力 API 模型后，capability range 显著拉宽。在纯 API 模型\n      （GPT-4o, Claude, Gemini）组成的 panel 中，所有成员 η 都很低（individual ASR\n      ~5-15%），η_max 方差小，回归中 η_max 的解释力下降（low variance → low signal）。\n      此时 K_eff 代表的模型多样性反而能捕捉到 residual attack surface 差异——\n      不同 API 模型对不同 attack type 的脆弱面不同，diversity 确实提供了互补保护。\n      但在包含弱模型（7B open-source）的 panel 中，某个模型 η ≈ 0.6-0.8，\n      远高于其他成员，weakest-link 效应依然成立。总体来看 η_max 显著率从 MVP 的\n      67%（4/6）下降到 42%（5/12），K_eff 从 0/6 显著负变为 4/12——\n      weakest-link theorem 不再 universal，而是 regime-dependent。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Multivariate regression results on 455 panels (15 models, K=3)\"\n        columns: [\"Dataset\", \"Attack\", \"β(η_max)\", \"p(η_max)\", \"β(K_eff)\", \"p(K_eff)\", \"R²\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"MMLU\", \"prompt-injection\", \"0.82\", \"0.003\", \"-0.31\", \"0.08\", \"0.34\"]\n          - [\"MMLU\", \"score-manipulation\", \"0.74\", \"0.011\", \"-0.22\", \"0.18\", \"0.26\"]\n          - [\"MMLU\", \"sycophancy\", \"0.58\", \"0.042\", \"-0.41\", \"0.03\", \"0.28\"]\n          - [\"MMLU\", \"verbosity\", \"0.45\", \"0.12\", \"-0.15\", \"0.42\", \"0.14\"]\n          - [\"MMLU\", \"position\", \"0.39\", \"0.18\", \"0.12\", \"0.51\", \"0.09\"]\n          - [\"MMLU\", \"authority\", \"0.68\", \"0.008\", \"-0.28\", \"0.11\", \"0.29\"]\n          - [\"ARC\", \"prompt-injection\", \"0.71\", \"0.015\", \"-0.38\", \"0.04\", \"0.31\"]\n          - [\"ARC\", \"score-manipulation\", \"0.63\", \"0.028\", \"-0.19\", \"0.27\", \"0.22\"]\n          - [\"ARC\", \"sycophancy\", \"0.52\", \"0.065\", \"-0.44\", \"0.02\", \"0.25\"]\n          - [\"ARC\", \"verbosity\", \"0.41\", \"0.14\", \"-0.33\", \"0.07\", \"0.18\"]\n          - [\"ARC\", \"position\", \"0.33\", \"0.22\", \"0.18\", \"0.35\", \"0.08\"]\n          - [\"ARC\", \"authority\", \"0.55\", \"0.052\", \"-0.26\", \"0.15\", \"0.21\"]\n      - caption: \"Regime-stratified η_max significance (panel capability tiers)\"\n        columns: [\"Panel Tier\", \"N panels\", \"η_max sig rate\", \"K_eff sig negative rate\", \"Median R²\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"All-API (GPT/Claude/Gemini)\", \"20\", \"0.17\", \"0.50\", \"0.12\"]\n          - [\"Mixed (API + 70B)\", \"120\", \"0.33\", \"0.42\", \"0.19\"]\n          - [\"All-large-OS (70B class)\", \"35\", \"0.50\", \"0.25\", \"0.24\"]\n          - [\"Mixed (large + small OS)\", \"180\", \"0.58\", \"0.17\", \"0.28\"]\n          - [\"All-small-OS (7B class)\", \"10\", \"0.67\", \"0.08\", \"0.35\"]\n          - [\"Contains ≥1 weak model\", \"280\", \"0.55\", \"0.18\", \"0.27\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: 12 conditions × 2 predictors (η_max, K_eff) showing p-values. Clear diagonal pattern — η_max cells darker (more significant) for targeted attacks (prompt-injection, score-manipulation), K_eff cells darker for shared-bias attacks (sycophancy) but only in strong-model panels.\"\n      - \"Scatter: panel min-capability (x) vs η_max significance (y, binary). Logistic regression overlay shows threshold around 70B-class capability where η_max transitions from dominant to non-significant.\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst 档最核心的结果变化。MVP 阶段的 6 模型结论（η_max dominates universally）\n      在 15 模型池上碎片化为 regime-dependent 结论。关键发现：(1) 强模型 panel\n      中 η_max 方差太小，不构成 weakest link——因为没有 weak link；(2) 此时\n      K_eff 代表的 diversity 确实提供了互补保护；(3) 弱模型 panel 中 MVP 结论完全成立。\n      论文 reframe 方向：从 \"η_max always dominates\" 变为 \"η_max dominates when\n      there exists a sufficiently weak member; above a capability threshold, diversity\n      becomes the operative defense\"。这实际上是更有趣的 nuanced result，但需要\n      reviewer 接受 regime-dependent 结论的价值。\n\n  - name: \"Attack expansion: 6+ attack types\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: >\n      新增 few-shot hijacking、persona manipulation、instruction override 三种攻击，\n      在 15+ 模型池上运行，验证 weakest-link 在更广泛 attack surface 上的表现。\n    expected_results:\n      new_attack_types: 3\n      total_attack_types: 9\n      total_conditions: 18  # 2 datasets × 9 attacks\n      eta_max_sig_rate_new_attacks: 0.33  # 2/6 new conditions\n      keff_sig_negative_rate_new_attacks: 0.50  # 3/6 new conditions\n      eta_max_sig_rate_overall: 0.39  # 7/18\n      keff_sig_negative_rate_overall: 0.39  # 7/18\n      few_shot_hijacking_eta_max_p: 0.19\n      few_shot_hijacking_keff_p: 0.04\n      persona_manipulation_eta_max_p: 0.035\n      persona_manipulation_keff_p: 0.22\n      instruction_override_eta_max_p: 0.08\n      instruction_override_keff_p: 0.03\n    result_rationale: >\n      新增攻击类型进一步分裂 weakest-link 的 universality。few-shot hijacking 和\n      instruction override 是高度 transferable 的攻击——它们利用 instruction-following\n      这一所有 LLM 共享的特性，因此对 panel 中所有模型的 ASR 较均匀。此时 η_max\n      解释力弱（因为 variance across judges 低），而 K_eff 反而显著——多样性意味着\n      不同模型对 instruction-following exploit 的具体 failure mode 不同，提供互补保护。\n      persona manipulation 类似 sycophancy，更依赖 individual model 特性（某些模型\n      对 authority cues 特别敏感），η_max 仍显著。总体上 η_max 和 K_eff 各在约 40%\n      条件下显著，无一方 universal dominate——核心 claim 需要 nuance。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Regression results for new attack types (455 panels)\"\n        columns: [\"Dataset\", \"Attack\", \"β(η_max)\", \"p(η_max)\", \"β(K_eff)\", \"p(K_eff)\", \"R²\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"MMLU\", \"few-shot-hijacking\", \"0.28\", \"0.24\", \"-0.48\", \"0.03\", \"0.19\"]\n          - [\"MMLU\", \"persona-manipulation\", \"0.72\", \"0.009\", \"-0.14\", \"0.39\", \"0.25\"]\n          - [\"MMLU\", \"instruction-override\", \"0.35\", \"0.15\", \"-0.52\", \"0.02\", \"0.22\"]\n          - [\"ARC\", \"few-shot-hijacking\", \"0.31\", \"0.19\", \"-0.39\", \"0.05\", \"0.16\"]\n          - [\"ARC\", \"persona-manipulation\", \"0.65\", \"0.035\", \"-0.21\", \"0.22\", \"0.22\"]\n          - [\"ARC\", \"instruction-override\", \"0.38\", \"0.12\", \"-0.44\", \"0.03\", \"0.20\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: attack type (x) vs η_max significance (blue) and K_eff significance (orange), grouped. Shows clear pattern — targeted attacks (prompt-injection, persona) favor η_max; transferable attacks (few-shot-hijacking, instruction-override, sycophancy) favor K_eff.\"\n    analysis: >\n      攻击扩展进一步确认 regime-dependent 结论，且揭示了一个有价值的 pattern：\n      attack transferability 是决定 η_max vs K_eff 哪个更重要的关键维度。\n      targeted attacks（需要针对特定模型调优的攻击）→ η_max 主导；\n      transferable attacks（利用 LLM 共性弱点的攻击）→ K_eff 有效。\n      这为 framework paper 提供了 regime characterization 的第二个维度\n      （第一个是 panel capability tier），增强了 analytical contribution。\n\n  - name: \"Adaptive adversary formal theorem + random-fault simulation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: >\n      (a) 形式化定理：adaptive adversary 下 panel_ASR = Θ(η_max)；\n      (b) random-fault simulation：每个 judge 独立以概率 p_j fail；\n      (c) 对比验证 BFT 区分。\n    expected_results:\n      theorem_holds: true\n      theorem_tightness: \"loose in strong-model regime\"\n      random_fault_keff_sig_rate: 0.39  # 7/18 conditions\n      adaptive_keff_sig_rate: 0.39\n      bft_contrast_cohen_d: 0.22\n      bft_contrast_p: 0.08\n      keff_beta_ratio_random_vs_adaptive: 1.4\n      random_fault_keff_median_beta: -0.52\n      adaptive_keff_median_beta: -0.37\n      regime_interaction_p: 0.04  # regime × fault-type interaction\n    result_rationale: >\n      形式化定理本身在数学上成立——在 adaptive adversary 假设下，panel ASR 的\n      upper bound 确实由 max(η_j) 决定。但在 worst 档下，实证数据显示这个 bound\n      在强模型 regime 中很 loose（实际 ASR 远低于 η_max bound），因为即使是\n      adaptive adversary，当所有模型都很强时，攻击成本太高，实际行为更接近\n      opportunistic 而非 truly adaptive。random-fault simulation 中 K_eff 确实\n      比 adaptive 条件下更显著，但差异不大（Cohen's d ≈ 0.22，远小于预期的\n      0.5+）——因为在实际数据中，即使是 adaptive attacks 也不完美 adaptive\n      （attacker 没有完美的 per-judge oracle），与 random fault 的差距没有\n      理论预测的那么大。关键的 saving grace 是 regime × fault-type 交互显著\n      （p=0.04）：在弱模型 panel 中 adaptive vs random 差异大，强模型 panel 中\n      差异消失。这支持 regime characterization 的 narrative。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"K_eff significance: adaptive vs random-fault across regimes\"\n        columns: [\"Regime\", \"Fault Type\", \"K_eff β\", \"K_eff p\", \"η_max β\", \"η_max p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Weak panels\", \"adaptive\", \"-0.12\", \"0.48\", \"0.78\", \"0.004\"]\n          - [\"Weak panels\", \"random-fault\", \"-0.41\", \"0.03\", \"0.52\", \"0.06\"]\n          - [\"Mixed panels\", \"adaptive\", \"-0.28\", \"0.09\", \"0.55\", \"0.04\"]\n          - [\"Mixed panels\", \"random-fault\", \"-0.45\", \"0.02\", \"0.38\", \"0.11\"]\n          - [\"Strong panels\", \"adaptive\", \"-0.44\", \"0.02\", \"0.22\", \"0.31\"]\n          - [\"Strong panels\", \"random-fault\", \"-0.58\", \"0.005\", \"0.15\", \"0.48\"]\n      - caption: \"BFT contrast effect sizes\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Weak panels\", \"Mixed panels\", \"Strong panels\", \"Overall\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Cohen's d (K_eff β difference)\", \"0.38\", \"0.21\", \"0.12\", \"0.22\"]\n          - [\"p (paired t-test)\", \"0.04\", \"0.12\", \"0.41\", \"0.08\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: K_eff β under adaptive (red) vs random-fault (blue), stratified by panel regime. Gap shrinks from left (weak) to right (strong), visualizing the regime × fault-type interaction.\"\n    analysis: >\n      BFT 区分的理论贡献被削弱。Overall Cohen's d = 0.22 远低于 medium effect size\n      标准（0.5），且 overall p = 0.08 不显著。只有在 weak panel regime 中 contrast\n      才显著（d = 0.38, p = 0.04）。这意味着 \"adaptive adversary fundamentally\n      different from BFT\" 这个 claim 需要限定为 \"the distinction matters primarily\n      in weak-model settings\"。不过 regime × fault-type 交互效应本身是有趣的发现，\n      可以作为 framework 的 analytical insight。论文需要降低 BFT contrast 的 claim\n      强度，从 \"fundamental distinction\" 变为 \"regime-dependent distinction\"。\n\n  - name: \"Capability-matched validation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: >\n      在同一 capability tier 内（如全 7B 或全 70B），测试控制 η_max 方差后\n      K_eff 是否显著。如果 within-tier K_eff 显著 → diversity 在控制 capability\n      后确实有效。\n    expected_results:\n      tiers_tested: 3  # 7B, 70B, API\n      tier_7b_keff_sig_rate: 0.17  # 1/6 conditions\n      tier_7b_eta_max_sig_rate: 0.50\n      tier_70b_keff_sig_rate: 0.33  # 2/6\n      tier_70b_eta_max_sig_rate: 0.33\n      tier_api_keff_sig_rate: 0.50  # 3/6\n      tier_api_eta_max_sig_rate: 0.17\n      diversity_capability_r_overall: -0.41\n      diversity_capability_r_within_7b: -0.18\n      diversity_capability_r_within_70b: -0.08\n      diversity_capability_r_within_api: -0.05\n      within_tier_keff_overall_sig_rate: 0.33\n    result_rationale: >\n      控制 capability tier 后，η_max 方差被大幅压缩（within-tier models 能力接近），\n      回归中 η_max 的解释力下降。此时 K_eff 在部分条件下变得显著——特别是在\n      API tier 中（3/6 显著），因为 GPT-4o、Claude、Gemini 虽然 capability 相似，\n      但 vulnerability profile 显著不同（不同训练数据和 safety alignment 策略），\n      diversity 确实提供互补保护。70B tier 中 K_eff 中等显著（2/6），7B tier 中\n      仍不显著（1/6）——因为 7B 模型普遍 vulnerable，η_max 方差虽然 within-tier\n      较小但绝对值仍高，weakest-link 效应持续。\n      diversity-capability tradeoff 的 overall r 从 MVP 的 -0.8 降到 -0.41（加入\n      API 模型后 tradeoff 大幅减弱），within-tier r 接近 0（-0.05 to -0.18）——\n      tradeoff 主要是 cross-tier artifact（比较 7B 和 70B 当然 diversity 高但\n      capability 低），而非 fundamental constraint。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Within-tier regression: K_eff significance by capability tier\"\n        columns: [\"Tier\", \"N models\", \"N panels (K=3)\", \"η_max sig rate\", \"K_eff sig neg rate\", \"Median R²\", \"K_eff-η_max r\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"7B class\", \"5\", \"10\", \"0.50\", \"0.17\", \"0.18\", \"-0.18\"]\n          - [\"70B class\", \"4\", \"4\", \"0.33\", \"0.33\", \"0.15\", \"-0.08\"]\n          - [\"API models\", \"5\", \"10\", \"0.17\", \"0.50\", \"0.12\", \"-0.05\"]\n          - [\"Cross-tier (all)\", \"15\", \"455\", \"0.42\", \"0.33\", \"0.22\", \"-0.41\"]\n      - caption: \"Diversity-capability tradeoff decomposition\"\n        columns: [\"Scope\", \"Pearson r\", \"p-value\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Overall (15 models)\", \"-0.41\", \"0.003\", \"Moderate negative — driven by tier differences\"]\n          - [\"Within 7B\", \"-0.18\", \"0.38\", \"Not significant — no tradeoff within tier\"]\n          - [\"Within 70B\", \"-0.08\", \"0.72\", \"Not significant\"]\n          - [\"Within API\", \"-0.05\", \"0.81\", \"Not significant\"]\n          - [\"Open-source only (10 models)\", \"-0.72\", \"0.001\", \"Strong negative — ecosystem artifact\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot with color-coded tiers: K_eff (x) vs η_max (y) for all 455 panels. Within-tier points form horizontal clusters (no tradeoff), but cross-tier slope is steep negative. Regression lines: overall (dashed, slope=-0.41) vs within-tier (solid, near-flat).\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst 档最具杀伤力的结果。diversity-capability tradeoff（Claim 3）被\n      证实主要是 open-source ecosystem artifact，而非 fundamental constraint。\n      加入 API 模型后 overall r 从 -0.8 降到 -0.41，within-tier r 接近 0。\n      这意味着 \"diversity and security are structurally at odds\" 这个 strong claim\n      需要大幅限定为 \"in the current open-source ecosystem, where capability\n      strongly predicts robustness, pursuing diversity across capability tiers\n      introduces weaker models\"。同时 within-tier K_eff 显著率 33% 表明\n      diversity 在 controlled settings 中确实有效——进一步削弱 \"diversity is a trap\"\n      narrative。论文 reframe 必须诚实承认这一点。\n\n  - name: \"Two-stage panel design algorithm: full benchmark\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: >\n      实现 robustness-first 两阶段算法（先筛 η ≤ threshold，再最大化 K_eff），\n      对比 5 个 baseline 策略。在 15+ 模型池上 sweep threshold。\n    expected_results:\n      strategies_compared: 6\n      total_conditions: 18\n      two_stage_win_rate: 0.44  # wins in 8/18 conditions\n      min_eta_max_win_rate: 0.39  # 7/18\n      max_keff_win_rate: 0.33  # 6/18\n      strongest_k_win_rate: 0.50  # 9/18\n      random_win_rate: 0.06  # 1/18\n      max_family_div_win_rate: 0.11  # 2/18\n      two_stage_vs_strongest_k_p: 0.32\n      two_stage_mean_asr: 0.091\n      strongest_k_mean_asr: 0.082\n      threshold_sensitivity: \"high — optimal threshold varies by attack type\"\n      pareto_dominated_by_strongest_k: \"partially\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      两阶段算法在 worst 档下表现不突出，因为 (1) strongest-K 策略（直接选最强 K 个\n      模型）在强模型 regime 中已经接近最优——当 API 模型可用时，选 GPT-4o + Claude +\n      Gemini 既有高 robustness 又有 decent diversity（不同公司的模型自然 diverse）；\n      (2) 两阶段算法的 threshold 参数高度 attack-dependent——对 prompt injection\n      最优 threshold ≠ 对 sycophancy 最优 threshold——无法给出 universal 建议；\n      (3) 在弱模型 pool（纯 open-source 7B）中两阶段确实优于 max-K_eff，但\n      strongest-K 同样优于 max-K_eff，且不需要 threshold tuning。\n      win rate 0.44 略低于 strongest-K 的 0.50，且差异不显著（p=0.32）。\n      robustness-first 不 dominate，practical contribution 被削弱为 \"在缺乏 API\n      模型时的合理 heuristic\" 而非 \"universal optimal strategy\"。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Panel selection strategy benchmark (mean ASR, lower is better)\"\n        columns: [\"Strategy\", \"Mean ASR\", \"Median ASR\", \"Win rate\", \"vs Random p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Two-stage (ours)\", \"0.091\", \"0.078\", \"0.44\", \"0.001\"]\n          - [\"Strongest-K\", \"0.082\", \"0.071\", \"0.50\", \"<0.001\"]\n          - [\"Min-η_max\", \"0.095\", \"0.085\", \"0.39\", \"0.003\"]\n          - [\"Max-K_eff\", \"0.131\", \"0.118\", \"0.33\", \"0.02\"]\n          - [\"Max-family-diversity\", \"0.158\", \"0.142\", \"0.11\", \"0.15\"]\n          - [\"Random\", \"0.172\", \"0.155\", \"0.06\", \"—\"]\n      - caption: \"Head-to-head: Two-stage vs Strongest-K by regime\"\n        columns: [\"Regime\", \"Two-stage wins\", \"Strongest-K wins\", \"Tie\", \"p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Weak panels (OS-7B only)\", \"4/6\", \"2/6\", \"0\", \"0.12\"]\n          - [\"Mixed panels\", \"3/6\", \"3/6\", \"0\", \"0.82\"]\n          - [\"Strong panels (API available)\", \"1/6\", \"4/6\", \"1\", \"0.08\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Pareto frontier plot: mean ASR (y, lower better) vs computational cost (x, lower better). Two-stage and Strongest-K both on frontier but at different points. Max-K_eff and Random clearly dominated.\"\n    analysis: >\n      两阶段算法没有显著优势，Claim 6 实质性削弱。strongest-K 策略在有 API 模型\n      可用时 win rate 更高，且不需要 threshold 参数。两阶段算法唯一优势场景是\n      纯 open-source weak model pool（4/6 wins），但这一场景在实践中正在减少\n      （API 模型越来越便宜易用）。practical contribution 从 \"robustness-first\n      algorithm dominates\" 降级为 \"when restricted to weak model pools, a\n      robustness-first heuristic helps, but is unnecessary when strong models\n      are available\"。可以在 paper 中作为 minor practical insight 保留，\n      但不能作为主要 contribution。\n\n  - name: \"Per-judge ASR concentration analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: >\n      对每个 panel × attack，测量 per-judge ASR 分布的集中度（Gini 系数、熵），\n      验证攻击是否集中在最弱 judge 上。\n    expected_results:\n      median_gini: 0.31\n      mean_gini: 0.34\n      gini_strong_panels: 0.18\n      gini_weak_panels: 0.52\n      gini_mixed_panels: 0.38\n      entropy_normalized_median: 0.78  # 1.0 = uniform, lower = more concentrated\n      concentration_on_weakest_fraction: 0.48  # fraction of successes on weakest judge\n      concentration_on_weakest_strong_panels: 0.38\n      concentration_on_weakest_weak_panels: 0.61\n      gini_adaptive_vs_random_p: 0.06\n      gini_adaptive_vs_random_d: 0.28\n    result_rationale: >\n      Per-judge ASR 集中度呈现清晰的 regime 分裂。在 weak panel（包含 7B 模型）中，\n      Gini ≈ 0.52，最弱 judge 承担 61% 的攻击成功——符合 adaptive adversary targeting\n      预测。但在 strong panel（全 API 模型）中，Gini ≈ 0.18，接近均匀分布——\n      攻击成功较均匀地分布在各 judge 上，因为没有明显的 \"weakest link\" 可供集中攻击。\n      adaptive vs random-fault 的 Gini 差异不显著（p=0.06, d=0.28）——因为即使在\n      adaptive 条件下，当模型能力相近时，attacker 的 targeting 精度有限，行为\n      接近 semi-random。这进一步支持 \"adaptive adversary distinction matters\n      primarily in weak-model regime\" 的结论。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Per-judge ASR concentration by panel regime\"\n        columns: [\"Regime\", \"Median Gini\", \"Mean entropy (norm.)\", \"Weakest-judge share\", \"N panels\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"All-API\", \"0.18\", \"0.91\", \"0.38\", \"20\"]\n          - [\"Mixed (API+70B)\", \"0.28\", \"0.83\", \"0.42\", \"120\"]\n          - [\"All-large-OS\", \"0.35\", \"0.77\", \"0.47\", \"35\"]\n          - [\"Mixed (large+small OS)\", \"0.45\", \"0.69\", \"0.55\", \"180\"]\n          - [\"All-small-OS\", \"0.52\", \"0.62\", \"0.61\", \"10\"]\n      - caption: \"Concentration: adaptive vs random-fault\"\n        columns: [\"Fault Type\", \"Median Gini\", \"Weakest-judge share\", \"Paired diff p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Adaptive\", \"0.34\", \"0.48\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Random-fault\", \"0.26\", \"0.41\", \"0.06\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Violin plot: Gini coefficient distribution, stratified by panel regime (x) and colored by fault type (adaptive=red, random=blue). Weak panels show high Gini with clear adaptive-random separation; strong panels show low Gini with overlapping distributions.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Concentration analysis 部分支持 adaptive adversary narrative，但仅限于\n      weak panel regime。在 strong panels 中，ASR 近乎均匀分布——不存在 \"weakest\n      link\" targeting 行为。这从另一个角度确认 regime-dependent 结论：adaptive\n      adversary model 的 descriptive accuracy 本身也是 regime-dependent 的。\n      在强模型 panel 中，adversary 更像 \"均匀探测\" 而非 \"精准打击\"。\n      这对形式化定理没有影响（定理给出 upper bound，不要求 tight），但削弱了\n      \"adaptive adversary is the right threat model\" 的 empirical support。\n\n  - name: \"Diversity-capability tradeoff visualization\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: >\n      在 C(15,3)=455 panels 上绘制 K_eff vs η_max scatter，拟合 tradeoff 曲线，\n      展示 Pareto frontier，按 capability tier 分层。\n    expected_results:\n      overall_pearson_r: -0.41\n      overall_spearman_r: -0.38\n      pareto_front_size: 12  # panels on Pareto frontier\n      pareto_composition: \"8/12 contain ≥2 API models\"\n      tradeoff_slope: -0.33\n      tradeoff_R2: 0.17\n      api_inclusive_r: -0.22\n      opensource_only_r: -0.72\n      pareto_panels_mean_asr: 0.075\n      non_pareto_mean_asr: 0.148\n    result_rationale: >\n      可视化清晰展示 tradeoff 的 ecosystem-dependent 本质。在纯 open-source 空间中，\n      K_eff vs η_max 呈强负相关（r=-0.72）：要 diversity 就必须跨 capability tier\n      混搭（如 7B + 70B），必然引入弱模型。但加入 API 模型后，右上角出现一个\n      \"sweet spot\" 区域——API 模型组合同时实现高 K_eff（不同公司模型自然 diverse）\n      和低 η_max（都很强）。Pareto frontier 被 API-inclusive panels 主导（8/12），\n      表明 tradeoff 可以通过使用 strong diverse models 打破。\n      Overall R² = 0.17 表明 tradeoff 只解释 17% 的方差——远非 \"structural\"。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Tradeoff statistics by model pool composition\"\n        columns: [\"Pool\", \"N panels\", \"r(K_eff, η_max)\", \"p\", \"R²\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"All 15 models\", \"455\", \"-0.41\", \"0.003\", \"0.17\", \"Moderate — not structural\"]\n          - [\"Open-source only (10)\", \"120\", \"-0.72\", \"<0.001\", \"0.52\", \"Strong — ecosystem artifact\"]\n          - [\"API-inclusive (≥1 API)\", \"335\", \"-0.22\", \"0.04\", \"0.05\", \"Weak — API breaks tradeoff\"]\n          - [\"All-API (5)\", \"10\", \"-0.05\", \"0.89\", \"0.003\", \"None — diversity is free\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Main scatter: K_eff (x) vs η_max (y) for 455 panels, colored by tier composition (blue=all-API, green=mixed, red=all-OS-weak). Pareto frontier highlighted. Two regression lines: overall (dashed, r=-0.41) and open-source-only (dotted, r=-0.72). Clear visual that API models break the tradeoff.\"\n      - \"Inset: K_eff (x) vs mean panel ASR (y) for Pareto-optimal panels only, showing that the 'diversity tax' disappears on the frontier.\"\n    analysis: >\n      可视化是 reframed paper 的关键 figure。它同时传达两个信息：(1) open-source\n      ecosystem 中 tradeoff 确实存在且严重（r=-0.72）；(2) 这不是 fundamental\n      constraint——API 模型的加入打破了 tradeoff。实际含义：diversity-as-defense\n      不是 inherently flawed，只是在当前 open-source 生态中因 capability 分层\n      严重而表现为 trap。随着 open-source 模型 capability 提升（如未来 7B 模型\n      接近当前 70B 水平），tradeoff 将进一步缩小。这是一个 more nuanced 且\n      arguably more useful 的 finding，但比 \"diversity is fundamentally a trap\"\n      的 punch 力弱很多。\n\n  - name: \"Panel size sensitivity: K=3,5,7,9\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: >\n      在不同 panel size (K=3,5,7,9) 下测试 weakest-link theorem。验证 η_max\n      dominance 是否随 K 增大而变化。\n    expected_results:\n      k3_eta_max_sig_rate: 0.42\n      k5_eta_max_sig_rate: 0.33\n      k7_eta_max_sig_rate: 0.28\n      k9_eta_max_sig_rate: 0.22\n      k3_keff_sig_negative_rate: 0.33\n      k5_keff_sig_negative_rate: 0.39\n      k7_keff_sig_negative_rate: 0.50\n      k9_keff_sig_negative_rate: 0.56\n      eta_max_sig_trend_p: 0.03  # linear trend test\n      keff_sig_trend_p: 0.02\n      k9_median_asr_reduction_vs_k3: 0.35  # 35% lower ASR\n      diversity_benefit_threshold_k: 5  # K at which K_eff becomes more often significant than η_max\n    result_rationale: >\n      随着 panel size 增大，两个效应叠加削弱 weakest-link：(1) 更多 judges 意味着\n      更大的 voting majority 需要被 flip，即使 weakest judge 被攻破，其 1 票在\n      K=9 的 majority-vote 中影响更小（1/9 vs 1/3）；(2) 大 panel 更可能包含\n      strong models（15 个模型中选 9 个 vs 选 3 个），η_max 的绝对值被拉低，\n      方差也更小。因此 η_max 显著率从 K=3 的 42% 单调下降到 K=9 的 22%，\n      而 K_eff 显著率从 33% 上升到 56%。在 K ≈ 5 时出现交叉——diversity\n      开始比 individual robustness 更重要。这对 practical recommendation\n      有直接影响：K=3 时 focus on robustness，K≥5 时 diversity matters。\n      但这也进一步削弱了 \"weakest-link is universal\" 的 claim——它甚至\n      不对所有 panel size universal。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Weakest-link persistence across panel sizes\"\n        columns: [\"K\", \"N panels\", \"η_max sig rate\", \"K_eff sig neg rate\", \"Median R²\", \"Mean ASR\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"3\", \"455\", \"0.42\", \"0.33\", \"0.22\", \"0.134\"]\n          - [\"5\", \"3003\", \"0.33\", \"0.39\", \"0.18\", \"0.105\"]\n          - [\"7\", \"6435\", \"0.28\", \"0.50\", \"0.15\", \"0.092\"]\n          - [\"9\", \"5005\", \"0.22\", \"0.56\", \"0.13\", \"0.087\"]\n      - caption: \"Transition analysis: K at which K_eff overtakes η_max\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"K=3\", \"K=5\", \"K=7\", \"K=9\", \"Trend p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"η_max sig rate\", \"0.42\", \"0.33\", \"0.28\", \"0.22\", \"0.03\"]\n          - [\"K_eff sig neg rate\", \"0.33\", \"0.39\", \"0.50\", \"0.56\", \"0.02\"]\n          - [\"η_max > K_eff (conditions)\", \"7/18\", \"6/18\", \"4/18\", \"3/18\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: panel size K (x) vs significance rate (y), two lines — η_max (red, decreasing) and K_eff (blue, increasing). Crossover at K≈5 highlighted. Shaded 95% CI bands.\"\n      - \"Box plot: panel ASR distribution by K, showing monotonic decrease with increasing K — diversity does provide aggregate protection at scale.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Panel size sensitivity 是最终确认 weakest-link non-universality 的实验。\n      η_max 显著率随 K 单调下降（0.42→0.22），K_eff 单调上升（0.33→0.56），\n      交叉在 K≈5。这有一个直觉解释：K=3 majority vote 中 1 个被攻破的 judge\n      已经占 1/3 的权重，weakest link 影响巨大；K=9 中 1/9 权重，需要同时\n      攻破 5 个 judge 才能 flip panel，此时 diversity（不同 judge 的 failure\n      mode 不同）确实提供了实质保护。\n      对 paper 的影响：weakest-link theorem 需要 qualified as \"primarily applies\n      to small panels (K≤5) and when panel includes sufficiently weak members\"。\n      Practical recommendation 变为 regime-dependent guidance：小 panel 重\n      robustness，大 panel 重 diversity。这对 framework paper narrative 实际上\n      是 positive——提供了一个清晰的、可操作的 regime boundary。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4e33aa2a-59d4-47c4-aaca-9a37046ba48e","total_cost_usd":0.43331525,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16777,"cache_read_input_tokens":53906,"output_tokens":11892,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16777,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":11723,"cache_read_input_tokens":21103,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7515,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7515},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4081,"outputTokens":21,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0041860000000000005,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":11892,"cacheReadInputTokens":53906,"cacheCreationInputTokens":16777,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.42912925,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"cfe88b8f-99fe-4018-8421-128960db9877"}
